S 14A.1 Reporting institutions are required to conduct CDD on customers and persons conducting the transaction, when:
(a) establishing business relations;
(b) providing money-changing and wholesale currency business;
(c) providing wire transfer services;
(d) providing electronic-money (e-money);
(e) carrying out occasional transactions involving an amount equivalent to RM25,000 and above, including in situations where the transaction is carried out in a single transaction or through several transactions in a day that appear to be linked;
(f) carrying out cash transactions involving an amount equivalent to RM25,000 and above;
(g) it has any suspicion of ML/TF/PF, regardless of amount; or
(h) it has any doubt about the veracity or adequacy of previously obtained information.

